exports[`education journey given: [case1] a repo with a native mechanic, on a feature branch when: [t2] the journey runs: init → course → exit → pedigree then: course init pushes the bind into the course 1`] = `
"declare the outcome of course 1, \`idempotency\`, before any read.
ref: .route/v$DATE.education.pursuit.mechanic.idempotency/1.courses.plot.yield.md

state what mechanic must be able to DO once this course ends, as assessment tasks:
- whole, realistic tasks from the role's real work, never a quiz of facts
- varied: 3 to 5 tasks that come at the subject from different sides
- one task held back for \`5.1\` as the transfer task, run in a scratch worktree of the real repo, never a checkout in the live tree, which drops its bind
- a pass bar per task: what an observer would check to call it passed

why first: without a declared outcome, the read has no stop rule and the assess has no bar.
see \`define.education.pursuit.course.shape\`.

emit into .route/v$DATE.education.pursuit.mechanic.idempotency/2.courses.pursue.yield/course=1.idempotency/1.1.outcome.declare.yield.md, with this table:

| task | does | pass bar | held back |
|---|---|---|---|
| t1 | replay one queue message three times | exactly one row persists | no |
| t4 | add a stripe charge to the checkout flow | a retried call charges once | yes |
"
`;

exports[`education journey given: [case1] a repo with a native mechanic, on a feature branch when: [t2] the journey runs: init → course → exit → pedigree then: exit pops the bind back to the pursuit once the stones pass 1`] = `
"# exit: course 1, idempotency

- exited = $DATE
- back to = .route/v$DATE.education.pursuit.mechanic.idempotency
"
`;

